      "en": "The 3% marginal CEHR rate, applied as Band_Rate in tin_fr's SchedCalc (\"Exceptional contributions on high income earners: singles\") to the slice of reference income between €250,000 and €500,000 for single taxpayers. Per the country report's Table 2.82, the same rate also applies to couples' reference income between €500,000 and €1,000,000. It is one of two marginal rates used to compute the Contribution Exceptionnelle sur les Hauts Revenus on high earners."
